WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.072 --> 00:00:02.368
-Welcome back
to "The Tonight Show"!

00:00:02.368 --> 00:00:03.837
We're hanging out
with Blake Shelton.

00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:05.839
It's time for
"The Jinx Challenge."

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:07.407
Here we go.

00:00:07.407 --> 00:00:10.977
♪ Jinx ♪
♪ J-J-Jinx Challenge ♪

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:13.446
-Now, to play this game,
we're each gonna need a partner.

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:15.714
On Blake's team,
please welcome fellow coach

00:00:15.714 --> 00:00:18.617
and our buddy on "The Voice,"
Kelly Clarkson!

00:00:18.617 --> 00:00:20.252
Yeah!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.252 --> 00:00:22.555
Come on, now!
Yes!

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:25.158
Oh, I'm so happy.
I will be playing with

00:00:25.158 --> 00:00:27.593
the one and only Tariq Trotter,
right here!

00:00:27.593 --> 00:00:31.130
♪♪

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:33.833
Now here's how it works.
We're gonna test just how strong

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:35.801
your connection is
to your teammate.

00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:36.903
Okay?
We're gonna take turns.

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:38.238
-He played with him last time.
-Yeah.

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:40.039
Y'all played together,
so this is not fair.

00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:41.674
-Yeah, y'all have,
like, a thing.

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:44.177
-We're gonna take turns
getting a category

00:00:44.177 --> 00:00:46.079
that will appear on the screen.
When you make --

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:48.547
Then you'll make eye contact
with your teammate.

00:00:48.547 --> 00:00:50.283
-Okay.
-You'll both count to three,

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:53.152
and then both say something from
that category at the same time.

00:00:53.152 --> 00:00:54.954
If you say the same thing,

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:56.923
it's a jinx,
and you get a point.

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:58.058
If you don't say the same thing,

00:00:58.058 --> 00:01:00.326
the other team
has a chance to steal.

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:02.328
Make sense, Blake?
Don't even -- just, yes.

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:03.729
Just say yes.
-Don't fail.

00:01:03.729 --> 00:01:05.565
-All right, now here we go.
-It's already a stupid game.

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:07.433
-Now, Tariq --
Please just don't say it.

00:01:07.433 --> 00:01:09.702
Blake, just -- you can think it,
just don't say it out loud.

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:11.204
Tariq and I are up first,

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:12.372
and we'll show you
how it's done.

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:15.108
What is the first category?

00:01:15.108 --> 00:01:16.809
Okay.
Olympic Event.

00:01:16.809 --> 00:01:19.379
Olympic -- Tariq,
you watch the Olympics, right?

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:21.680
-Mm-hmm.
-Olympic event, okay?

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:24.684
Think of an Olympic event.

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:26.886
One, two, three.

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:27.987
-Javelin.
-Gymnastics!

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:30.557
What?! Javelin?
Did you say javelin?

00:01:30.557 --> 00:01:32.492
Did you think it was javelin?
-Javelin.

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:35.361
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:36.629
-Okay, let's win.
-Here we go, guys.

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:40.132
You make eye contact.
-Okay.

00:01:40.132 --> 00:01:41.667
Then do we count?
-Yeah, you count.

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:44.336
-Okay, okay.
One, two, three.

00:01:44.336 --> 00:01:45.604
-Archery.
-Curling.

00:01:45.604 --> 00:01:46.906
-What?!
[ Buzzer ]

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:48.508
We're "The Voice."
-But I've done archery

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:49.775
on my own.
-Archery.

00:01:49.775 --> 00:01:51.110
-Archery?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:54.113
-We're not thinking of hunting!
-It said Olympics!

00:01:54.113 --> 00:01:56.149
-Archery?!
Okay, Robin Hood.

00:01:56.149 --> 00:01:57.784
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.784 --> 00:01:59.819
-Let's change -- Let's change
to a different subject.

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:01.120
With a different subject,
we'll try it again.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:02.855
-We're gonna fail.
-But this time, it's your turn.

00:02:02.855 --> 00:02:03.989
-Oh, my gosh.
-You guys go first.

00:02:03.989 --> 00:02:07.026
A different category.
The category is...

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:08.861
"Cowboy Accessory."

00:02:08.861 --> 00:02:12.264
What's a cowboy accessory?
You guys go.

00:02:12.264 --> 00:02:13.999
-Okay, a cowboy thing.
-Ready?

00:02:13.999 --> 00:02:16.068
-Okay.
One, two, three.

00:02:16.068 --> 00:02:17.203
-Horse.
-Spurs.

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:18.971
Spurs!
-What?

00:02:18.971 --> 00:02:20.572
A horse!
A horse?!

00:02:20.572 --> 00:02:24.042
-And she said spurs!
-Wait. Is a horse an accessory?

00:02:24.042 --> 00:02:25.477
What are you talking --
-Just because something happened

00:02:25.477 --> 00:02:27.480
with me and Suzie,
doesn't mean I'm thinking --

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:30.116
-I'm trying to do things
that connect to "The Voice."

00:02:30.116 --> 00:02:32.051
-What is a cowboy --
cowboy accessory.

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:34.420
Oh, my gosh. Ready?
-One, two, three!

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:35.421
-Chaps!
-Boots!

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:37.290
[ Buzzer ]
-What did you say?

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:40.126
-I heard boot.
-What did you say?

00:02:40.126 --> 00:02:42.728
-[ Laughing ]
Chaps.

00:02:42.728 --> 00:02:44.596
-Chaps?!
Oh, my God.

00:02:44.596 --> 00:02:46.966
[ Laughter and applause ]
-That's what I was gonna say.

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:49.602
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:52.305
-Cowboy -- Cowboy boots!

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:54.006
Chaps?!
-Spurs!

00:02:54.006 --> 00:02:55.307
See, Jimmy,
we're on the same --

00:02:55.307 --> 00:02:58.911
-Yes, boots, spurs.
You have one chance to steal.

00:02:58.911 --> 00:03:00.947
Name a cowboy accessory.

00:03:00.947 --> 00:03:03.049
Whenever you're ready,
count to three and say it.

00:03:03.049 --> 00:03:04.316
-One, two, three.

00:03:04.316 --> 00:03:05.351
-Rope.
-Rope.

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:06.786
-Yes!
[ Ding ]

00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:10.355
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:10.355 --> 00:03:12.758
Yes!
-A rope.

00:03:12.758 --> 00:03:14.060
-You gave --
We gave that one to them.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:15.995
-Cowboy accessory.
They both said rope.

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:17.463
-We gave that one to them.
-That's not an accessory.

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:20.099
-'Cause you rope the calf.
-This is all silly.

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:21.801
I've never even heard of this
in my lifetime.

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:23.569
-All right.
-Whatever, chaps.

00:03:23.569 --> 00:03:25.371
-Here we go.
Chaps.

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:27.306
All right. Now look,
this is the last one here.

00:03:27.306 --> 00:03:28.974
Whoever wins
this next category...

00:03:28.974 --> 00:03:31.910
[ Horn sound ]
...wins the whole thing.

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:35.548
-What is it?
-10,000 points, final round.

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:37.816
You guys will go first
just because you're our guests.

00:03:37.816 --> 00:03:39.618
You have a chance to win
the whole game right here.

00:03:39.618 --> 00:03:41.220
What is the category?
-You're damn right we do.

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:42.688
Okay.
-Damn right. Okay.

00:03:42.688 --> 00:03:45.258
-"States in the South."
All right, one, two, three.

00:03:45.258 --> 00:03:46.525
Whenever you're ready, go.
"States in the South."

00:03:46.525 --> 00:03:47.526
-No, no, wait!
What do you mean?

00:03:47.526 --> 00:03:48.694
What do you mean?
We just say them?

00:03:48.694 --> 00:03:50.296
-Here we go!
States in the South!

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:51.430
-Tennessee!
-Texas!

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:53.232
[ Laughter ]
-That's not in the South!

00:03:53.232 --> 00:03:55.301
That's in the West!
Where is that?

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:58.204
-Texas is in the South.
-I thought it was in the West.

00:03:58.204 --> 00:04:01.039
You live --
You live in Tennessee.

00:04:01.039 --> 00:04:02.675
-Straight down South.

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:04.810
-We got to think of another one.
Okay.

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:07.313
-Okay. I got it. Ready?

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:09.281
One, two, three.

00:04:09.281 --> 00:04:10.349
-Alabama.
-Ge--

00:04:10.349 --> 00:04:12.251
Oh, my God.
[ Buzzer ]

00:04:12.251 --> 00:04:15.554
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.554 --> 00:04:18.156
-What were you gonna say?
-I was gonna --

00:04:18.156 --> 00:04:19.359
-I was saying Georgia.

00:04:19.359 --> 00:04:21.560
I only got
the first syllable out, though.

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:23.596
-Blake, we're gonna pick --
we're gonna pick a --

00:04:23.596 --> 00:04:26.399
It's a state in the South.
-Yes, I'm going --

00:04:26.399 --> 00:04:30.069
It's way down South.
Here we go.

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:32.371
One, two, three.

00:04:32.371 --> 00:04:33.405
-Florida!
-Florida!

00:04:33.405 --> 00:04:35.942
[ Ding! ]
-Yes!

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:37.209
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:37.209 --> 00:04:38.210
♪♪

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:39.812
-We win!

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:46.819
♪♪

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:49.722
-My thanks to Blake Shelton,
Kelly Clarkson, Tariq Trotter!

00:04:49.722 --> 00:04:52.591
"The Voice,"
two-hour live season finale,

00:04:52.591 --> 00:04:55.762
airs next Monday and Tuesday
at 8:00 p.m., on NBC.

